245 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487245 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487245 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186487055 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487245 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bad153a8-2020-537a-b663-7fb9b6a11421" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487278 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487278 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487278 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487278 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487278 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487278 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487278 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487278 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186486681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487278 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f7933389-f875-5063-949e-56f9664cbd7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486641 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487279 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186487051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487279 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487279 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487279 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186486700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487279 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f7a4bfbe-757f-5eb8-9d00-cbed8edcec34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487281 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487281 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487281 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487281 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487281 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186487125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487281 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487281 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487281 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186486977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487281 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fac5256f-c4eb-5937-9a69-2c2d9a6f4b46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487333 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487333 #edb/ref 1069 "q-154662" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487333 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487333 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following equations has *no* solution?\n\nI. $|2x+1|-2=3$\n\nII. $|2x+1|=1$\n\nIII. $|2x+1|=-3$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487333 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5bd06631-7e99-59a6-a0d1-351c08d361fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487333 #edb/ref 1074 "An absolute value equation has no solution if, when the absolute value is isolated on the left side, the right-hand side is negative.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each equation in turn:\n\n- Equation I has a solution. To see this, we first isolate the absolute value on the left-hand side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2x+1|-2 & =3 \\\\ |2x+1| & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the right-hand side is non-negative, this equation has a solution.\n\n- Equation II has a solution. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is non-negative.\n\n- Equation III *has no solution*. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is *negative*.\n\nTherefore, the answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487339 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487339 #edb/ref 1069 "q-154635" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487339 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487339 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the absolute value equation \n\n$$\n5-|x-3|=-3.\n$$\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$$\n|x-3|=k\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $k?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487339 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "65b91c89-ea1f-5d94-8a2d-584db112f3d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487339 #edb/ref 1074 "We can rearrange the equation to isolate the absolute value on the left side:\n\nFirst, we subtract $5$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-|x-3|=-3 \\\\ 5-|x-3|-5=-3-5 \\\\ -|x-3|=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-|x-3| & =-8 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-|x-3|) & =(-1)\\cdot (-8) \\\\ (\\cancel{-}1)\\cdot (\\cancel{-}|x-3|) & =8 \\\\ |x-3| & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487342 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487342 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487342 #edb/ref 1069 "q-215513" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487342 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487342 #edb/ref 1071 "Written in ascending order, the solutions to $4-|2x-5|=3$ are $x=${{field-1}} \nand $x=$\n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487342 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "75db5801-eb7a-544e-9657-7c91f7a11bf0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487342 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-|2x-5| & =3 \\\\ -|2x-5| & =-1 \\\\ |2x-5| & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $|2x-5|=2x-5,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2x-5| & =1 \\\\ 2x-5 & =1 \\\\ 2x & =6 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|2x-5|=-(2x-5),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2x-5| & =1 \\\\ -(2x-5) & =1 \\\\ -2x+5 & =1 \\\\ -2x & =-4 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=2$ and $x=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487353 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487353 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75892" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487353 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487353 #edb/ref 1071 "If $2|5x-3|+1=15,$ then $x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487353 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99e6cc0a-d678-5e56-8a48-bdcbe16a46ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487353 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2|5x-3|+1 & =15 \\\\ 2|5x-3| & =14 \\\\ |5x-3| & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $|5x-3|=5x-3,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5x-3| & =7 \\\\ 5x-3 & =7 \\\\ 5x & =10 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|5x-3|=-(5x-3),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5x-3| & =7 \\\\ -(5x-3) & =7 \\\\ -5x+3 & =7 \\\\ -5x & =4 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{4}{5}$ and $x=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487365 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487365 #edb/ref 1069 "q-215504" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487365 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487365 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the absolute value equation \n\n$$\n-8|2x+1|+20=4.\n$$\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$|2x+1|=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487365 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aacab06e-bd32-550c-b949-9f30eb343d4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487365 #edb/ref 1074 "We can rearrange the equation to isolate the absolute value on the left side:\n\nFirst, we subtract $20$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8|2x+1|+20 & =4 \\\\ -8|2x+1|+20-20 & =4-20 \\\\ -8|2x+1| & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $-8:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8|2x+1| & =-16 \\\\ \\frac{-8|2x+1|}{-8} & =\\frac{-16}{-8} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-8}|2x+1|}{\\cancel{-8}} & =2 \\\\ |2x+1| & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487368 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487217 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487368 #edb/ref 1069 "q-215502" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487368 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487368 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the absolute value equation \n\n$$\n8-|4x+5|=1.\n$$\n\nThis equation can be expressed in the following equivalent form:\n\n$|4x+5|=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487368 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ad83e0ea-4391-59a0-adc0-7a2eea885dc7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487368 #edb/ref 1074 "We can rearrange the equation to isolate the absolute value on the left side:\n\nFirst, we subtract $8$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-|4x+5|=1 \\\\ 8-|4x+5|-8=1-8 \\\\ -|4x+5|=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-|4x+5| & =-7 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-|4x+5|) & =(-1)\\cdot (-7) \\\\ (\\cancel{-}1)\\cdot (\\cancel{-}|4x+5|) & =7 \\\\ |4x+5| & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487381 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487381 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75890" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487381 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487381 #edb/ref 1071 "If $|6-2b|+2=18,$ then $b=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487381 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c8460d4b-81b8-5707-a316-5df813e7f65d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487381 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|6-2b|+2 & =18 \\\\ |6-2b| & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $|6-2b|=6-2b,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|6-2b| & =16 \\\\ 6-2b & =16 \\\\ -2b & =10 \\\\ b & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|6-2b|=-(6-2b),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|6-2b| & =16 \\\\ -(6-2b) & =16 \\\\ 2b-6 & =16 \\\\ 2b & =22 \\\\ b & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $b=-5$ and $b=11.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487385 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487385 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487385 #edb/ref 1069 "q-215509" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487385 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487385 #edb/ref 1071 "Written in ascending order, the solutions to $|5-x|-8=7$ are $x=${{field-1}}\nand $x=$\n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487385 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d1182683-804f-5b60-aecd-25a7c3c4b698" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487385 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we isolate the absolute value on the left side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5-x|-8 & =7 \\\\ |5-x| & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following two cases:\n\n- If $|5-x|=5-x,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5-x| & =15 \\\\ 5-x & =15 \\\\ -x & =10 \\\\ x & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $|5-x|=-(5-x),$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|5-x| & =15 \\\\ -(5-x) & =15 \\\\ -5+x & =15 \\\\ x & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-10$ and $x=20.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487392 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487392 #edb/ref 1069 "q-154670" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487392 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487392 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following equations has *no* solution?\n\nI. $|5-x|=7$\n\nII. $1-|5-x|=5$\n\nIII. $|5-x|=-1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487392 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e251dfd2-42a3-5421-a165-7d060c5b7a7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487392 #edb/ref 1074 "An absolute value equation has no solution if, when the absolute value is isolated on the left side, the right-hand side is negative.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each equation in turn:\n\n- Equation I has a solution. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is non-negative.\n\n- Equation II *has no solution*. To see this, we first isolate the absolute value on the left-hand side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-|5-x| & =5 \\\\ -|5-x| & =4 \\\\ |5-x| & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the right-hand side is *negative*, this equation has *no* solution.\n\n- Equation III *has no solution*. The absolute value is already isolated on the left-hand side, and the right-hand side is *negative*.\n\nTherefore, the answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
